<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH PM SAYS SPENDING CUTS TO BE &quot;ALMOST 5PCT&quot;.</title>
<headline>CZECH PM SAYS SPENDING CUTS TO BE &quot;ALMOST 5PCT&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech Prime Minister Vaclav Klaus said on Wednesday that the government would make cuts to the state budget of almost five percent of originally planned expenditures.</p>
<p>Klaus, speaking as the cabinet was meeting over details of its planned pro-growth package, did not elaborate on any other details, saying they would be announced later on Wednesday. He later returned to the meeting.</p>
</text>
